From 881b00eb8f5b811ee5174517c05f1b1016f3ebf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:35:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-122: a new C++ event can no longer break the build
 -- the build's part goes to disk at once (0.122.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261001: "你這邊建置時 可能有問題" (+ the machine-side session's report). 08:46 an event added
in the designer (main.html sbCloseProgram.OnMouseDown) put six files in ONE unsaved edit, the generated
HtdEvents/HtdEvents.gen.cpp even as an untitled document; only four got saved, CMakeLists.txt named a
file that did not exist, and every F5 build failed (restored by that session on EastSun's ruling).
- The build's part goes straight to disk, in this order: HtdEvents.gen.cpp -> the CMakeLists.txt entry
  -> wb_serve.cpp's htd.event branch; stopped anywhere, the tree still builds. wb_serve.cpp and
  CMakeLists.txt are spliced byte by byte (lib/cppbridge.js spliceBytes; wb_serve.cpp has bytes that
  are not UTF-8, an editor's UTF-8 save would change them); the server's note is ASCII now.
- Every generated row calls its handler only when the class has it (decltype / SFINAE: C<i>(..., int)
  else C<i>(..., long) = 0): an unsaved / renamed / undone form .h / .cpp still compiles, the web gets
  "no-handler"; a null form object "no-form".
- One of those three files with unsaved text (or an old untitled tab) in an editor = nothing written,
  not wired, the reason said. Rename / reset write the table to disk too. The form's .h / .cpp and the
  page stay unsaved and undoable (WPF). hub.disk = the one door to disk (tests put memory there).

Checked: the generated file against the real tree (5 rows, 3 handlers missing) with WinLibs 16.2
-std=c++14 and MinGW.org 6.3 -std=c++1z, -fsyntax-only: 0 errors; a mock run 8/8 with both (exists =
called with the right args / sender; missing, private = no-handler; null = no-form; unknown row;
running). run_all 3/3 layers (lib 167, smoke 196): the write order, every other byte of the server and
CMake kept, the real tree untouched, an unsaved tab = nothing written. The real VS Code layer not run
(VS Code's own update still holds its lock); its test was moved to the in-memory disk too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
